Backport of the one compile fix trivy needs on Go 1.27, from upstream
aquasecurity/trivy dc3c56eed5 "chore: bump Go to 1.27 (#11127)" (2026-08-21,
on main; not in any release as of v0.74.0).

Go 1.27's encoding/json/v2 dropped `json.SkipFunc`; the "skip this custom
unmarshaler and fall back to default decoding" sentinel is now
`errors.ErrUnsupported`. Without this, v0.74.0 fails on Go 1.27.1 with
`pkg/x/json/json.go:109:16: undefined: json.SkipFunc` on both arches (pkgs#758).
Only json.go is taken; the rest of that upstream commit is CI/lint/test churn
and a style-only move to errors.AsType. Drop this patch at the next trivy
release (upstream main already carries it).

diff --git a/pkg/x/json/json.go b/pkg/x/json/json.go
--- a/pkg/x/json/json.go
+++ b/pkg/x/json/json.go
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ import (
 	"bytes"
 	"encoding/json/jsontext"
 	"encoding/json/v2"
+	"errors"
 	"io"
 
 	"golang.org/x/xerrors"
@@ -106,7 +107,8 @@ func unmarshaler[T any](r *lineReader, visited set.Set[int], hooks ...DecodeHook
 
 		// Check visited set to avoid infinity loops
 		if visited.Contains(start) {
-			return json.SkipFunc
+			// Fall back to the default decoding.
+			return errors.ErrUnsupported
 		}
 		visited.Append(start)
 
